  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The sequence repeats the nine-letter block \\(\\text{ABCDEDCBA}\\). Its last \\(A\\) is followed by the first \\(A\\) of the next block, accounting for the adjacent \\(A\\)'s in the displayed sequence.\n\nSince\n\\[\n1992=9\\cdot221+3,\n\\]\nthere are \\(221\\) complete blocks before the three remaining letters. The \\(1992\\)nd letter is therefore the third letter of the next block, which is \\(C\\). The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
